opentune-scan
=============

Part of the signature-based ECU recognition in `src/recognize/` re-implements,
in Rust and from scratch, ECU-identification knowledge documented by:

    openremap-core — https://github.com/v-arapidis/openremap-core
    (MIT License, revision 6c6ba852 consulted)

What was taken: public layout facts and marker strings that the openremap-core
extractors document, namely

  * Bosch ME7: the `ZZ` ident block at 0x10000 with a non-printable third byte
    (printable = Marelli ME1.5.5 style) and the ME7 family literals;
  * Bosch ME9/MED9: the `Bosch.Common.RamLoader.Me9` anchor and the MED9
    exclusion;
  * Bosch EDC16: the size → active-section table with `DE CA FE` at
    active+0x3D and the SW number at active+0x10;
  * Bosch EDC15: the `TSW` toolchain line and the C167 `PP22..00` bootstrap
    header;
  * Siemens/Continental: `5WP4` (Simos), `5WS4…-T` (SID), `5WK9…--…MS4x`
    (MS4x), `PPD1.x`/`CASN`/`111SN` (PPD), `CAPM3`/`111PM3` (SID801),
    `CAPO`/`111PO` (SID803) markers;
  * Delphi Multec's `0x11 "DEL"` header; Marelli `MAG`/MJD and `iaw` tags;
    the Denso `Copr.DENSO` / `Cpyr.DENSO` / `CopyrightDENSO` anchors;
  * the exclusion lists that keep those detectors disjoint.

What was NOT taken: no source code was copied or translated line by line;
OpenTune's detectors, the evidence/tier model, the Bosch project-descriptor
parser, the VAG ident-block parser, the Siemens calibration-header detector,
the SuperH reset-vector check, the Delphi copyright/MT/DCM literals and the
synthetic fixture generator are OpenTune's own. Explicitly excluded from use:
openremap-core's GS20/SMG2 checksum (derived from a decompiled tool), anything
it ported from GPL-2.0-only RomRaider (the Denso/Subaru checksum and ROM
tables), and all checksum algorithms. No firmware, calibration data or dumps
from any source are included.

